#!/usr/bin/env sh
# plan 2933 (fix A): warn when a raw `git rebase` / `git pull --rebase` is about to run on
# `master` in the SHARED MAIN checkout, outside the sanctioned pushMasterWithRebase path.
# A rebase killed there leaves MAIN detached with residue that heal-main.mjs SPARES for 15
# minutes (its mtime gate assumes a live operator hand-rebase), so every parallel session
# sees a wedged checkout. Measured 2026-08-06.
#
# EDIT-FROZEN DISPATCHER, same rule as .husky/pre-push (plan 2576): the logic lives in
# scripts/ because `.husky/**` is a path an unattended cloud drain can never Edit/Write
# (the harness safetyCheck has no approver and the session hangs until the window dies).
# Keeping this file trivial means it never needs another edit.
#
# ADVISORY ONLY. Unlike post-checkout, git DOES honour a pre-rebase hook's exit code — a
# non-zero exit ABORTS the rebase. The guard already always exits 0; `|| true` is the second
# belt so a guard crash (missing node, torn node_modules, a syntax error mid-edit) can never
# block the operator's rebase. Do not remove it, and do not make this hook blocking.
#
# git passes the hook <upstream> [<branch>]; forward them for future use.
node scripts/pre-rebase-main-guard.mjs "$@" || true
